mvvault: each listed entry is one `<li>` (checkpoint 4)

Draft, 2026-09-23, for mvvault v2 (v1 plus this). No judge run. The wording is a first pass.

An unwritten test assumption. The tests find each entry on the category listing by its link
and then take the link's enclosing `<li>`; the spec names no markup for the listing.

The tests. test_checkpoint_4.py `_entry_row` does `soup.find("a", href=...)`, then
`anchor.find_parent("li")`, and asserts the result is not None ("Missing list item for …").
Three tests go through it: test_v1_downloaded_mark, test_v3_downloaded_mark and
test_v3_removed_mark. Each then compares two rows' signatures (the `<li>`'s classes and text,
minus the title), so a downloaded or removed mark has to be inside the `<li>`. The reference
solution (solutions/checkpoint_4/mvault.py) renders `<ul>` of `<li>`.

The spec. checkpoint_4.md:63 "Listing Rules" says what a listing shows (order, current title,
downloaded state, "Visual distinction | Downloaded and undownloaded states must be
distinguishable", the v3 removed indicator) and "Entry navigation | Each listed entry includes a
link to `/catalog/<name>/<category>/<id>`". Nothing says list, list item or `<ul>`. A table
with one `<tr>` per entry meets every row.

The runs. bin/test-history: test_v1_downloaded_mark 19 pass, 2 fail. The two fails are the
sonnet-4.6 control (just-solve v0, 20260829T1910) and Opus 5.5 min13 on v1
(opus-5-5_2.1.280_high_min13-ABDJKMNT-specv1/20260923T0834), which rendered a `<table>`
(vaultlib/viewer/pages.py: one `<tr class=…>` per entry, the state marks as classes and cells).
All three tests fail together in both runs. No registry entry asks the question: the Opus 5.5
registry (74 entries) has none on listing markup. Nobody read it and chose wrong; the passing
runs chose `<li>` without being told.

Over-correction to avoid: naming `<ul>`, or classes, or where the marks go. The tests need only
that the link sits inside an `<li>` that also carries the entry's state; "one `<li>`" per
entry is what makes the marks land inside it. If that reads as too loose, "one `<li>` holding
its link and its marks" says it outright.

--- a/mvvault/checkpoint_4.md
+++ b/mvvault/checkpoint_4.md
@@ -72,7 +72,7 @@
 | Visual distinction | Downloaded and undownloaded states must be distinguishable |
 | Removed indicator (v3 only) | Entries with latest `removed` value `true` are visually distinct from active entries |
 | Removed indicator (v1/v2) | Not applicable; no `removed` field exists |
-| Entry navigation | Each listed entry includes a link to `/catalog/<name>/<category>/<id>` |
+| Entry navigation | Each `<li>` entry includes a link to `/catalog/<name>/<category>/<id>` |
 
